sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch01-05> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "The form of an object is a diagram of the forces acting or that have acted on it" ;
    dct:description "The form of any portion of matter, living or dead, can be read as a diagram of forces: from the shape of a solid one can deduce the forces that produced and maintain it, and from the shape of a fluid the forces currently acting on it, so an organism's conformation is explained by a balance of forces." ;
    delphi:context "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter I, “Introductory”; topic “Form as a diagram of forces”. Scope: living and non-living bodies, including whole organisms and cells" ;
    dct:type "mechanism" .
}

